 "issue": 1661,
 "issue_title": "Bug: ArFrame column selection methods drop attrs metadata",
 "issue_body": "## Summary\n\n`ArFrame` preserves pandas `DataFrame.attrs` through `from_pandas()` and `to_pandas()`, but column-selection methods on `ArFrame` drop that metadata.\n\nThis affects methods such as `select_columns()`, `drop_columns()`, and `select_dtypes()`, all of which construct `ArFrame(...)` without passing a copy of the source frame attrs.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nUsers may store provenance, owner, sensitivity tags, source system names, or run IDs in `DataFrame.attrs`. After converting into Arnio, basic column selection should not silently remove that metadata.\n\nThis is separate from native cleaning operations dropping attrs because these are core `ArFrame` methods.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `arnio/convert.py`: `from_pandas()` deep-copies pandas attrs into `ArFrame`.\n- `arnio/convert.py`: `to_pandas()` restores `ArFrame._attrs` to pandas output.\n- `arnio/frame.py`: `select_columns()` returns `ArFrame(self._frame.select_columns(columns))` with no attrs.\n- `arnio/frame.py`: `drop_columns()` returns `ArFrame(self._frame.select_columns(...))` with no attrs.\n- `arnio/frame.py`: `select_dtypes()` delegates to `select_columns()`, so it also drops attrs.\n\n## Reproduction or trigger\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport arnio as ar\n\nsource = pd.DataFrame({\"a\": [1, 2], \"b\": [3, 4]})\nsource.attrs = {\"source\": \"crm\"}\n\nframe = ar.from_pandas(source)\nprint(frame._attrs)\nprint(frame.select_columns([\"a\"])._attrs)\nprint(frame.drop_columns([\"b\"])._attrs)\nprint(frame.select_dtypes(include=\"int64\")._attrs)\n```\n\nCurrent behavior: the original frame has attrs, while selected frames have `{}`.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nNon-mutating column-selection operations should preserve a defensive copy of `frame._attrs` unless the project explicitly documents that metadata is intentionally discarded.\n\n## Actual behavior\n\nThe returned `ArFrame` objects have empty attrs.\n\n## Suggested direction\n\nAdd a small helper for wrapping derived native frames with copied attrs and use it in `ArFrame` selection methods. Add tests for:\n\n- `select_columns()` preserving attrs\n- `drop_columns()` preserving attrs\n- `select_dtypes()` preserving attrs through selection\n- deep-copy isolation so nested attrs are not shared unexpectedly\n\n## References\n\n- `arnio/frame.py`\n- `arnio/convert.py`\n- Related but separate issue: native cleaning wrappers dropping attrs metadata\r\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/1661",
 "pr": 1999,
